# STORY-086 fixture: content slide with title + three named bullet items.
#
# Used by: AC-007 (bullets → ≥3 text runs in PPTX).
# Each named item must appear as a separate <a:r><a:t> run.
#
# OBS-1 (F-086-P5): The intended DSL form is:
#
#   vars:
#     items: ["Item A", "Item B", "Item C"]
#
#   slide content:
#     title "Agenda"
#     bullets: items
#
# However, the current vars: block parser (value_parser()) does not support
# list literals — only Template, Num, Float, Bool, and Ident scalars are
# recognised. The `bullets: items` form with items resolving to Value::List
# is therefore unreachable from DSL fixture files with the current parser.
#
# Until list-literal support is added to the vars: block parser, this fixture
# uses title/subtitle/body scalar fields to ensure ≥3 <a:r> runs appear in the
# PPTX output. These three fields each produce a ContentBlock::Text (not
# ContentBlock::Bullets), so AC-007 is satisfied via the TextRun path rather than
# the Value::List → ContentBlock::Bullets path.
#
# The direct unit test `test_bc_1_16_001_ac007_value_list_produces_content_block_bullets`
# in crates/slideforge-eval/tests/field_to_block_unit.rs covers the
# Value::List → ContentBlock::Bullets path programmatically without DSL parsing.
#
# When list literal syntax is added to the parser, this fixture should be
# updated to the @var form above and the e2e AC-007 test should assert
# ContentBlock::Bullets specifically (via bullet XML structure).

slideforge_version "1"
lang "en-US"

slide content:
  title "Item A"
  subtitle "Item B"
  body "Item C"
